---
// How the verdict is withheld (spec §9 item 7a): the real mechanism of decisions 0013, 0016 and
// 0077, drawn in HTML and CSS, without script, top to bottom so it fits a phone. A screen reader
// reads it as ordered lists. The guard's five checks beneath are worded from
// records/split.py and records/guard.py, not from the spec's draft (plan step 5, Task 4).
import { repoUrl } from "../lib/words";

const DECISIONS = "docs/decisions/";
const d0013 = repoUrl(`${DECISIONS}0013-evidence-synthesis-verdict.md`);
const d0016 = repoUrl(`${DECISIONS}0016-layered-leakage-guard-and-model-boundary.md`);
const d0077 = repoUrl(`${DECISIONS}0077-analysis-sentences-in-docket-documents-mark-the-case.md`);
---

<figure class="split">
    <ol class="flow" aria-label="How one case reaches the agent">
        <li class="box">One case: the NTSB's record and its docket</li>
        <li class="box key">
            The split: one function, <code>split_record</code>, the only place a record is divided
        </li>
        <li>
            <ol class="routes" aria-label="The three parts">
                <li>
                    <ol class="route" aria-label="Evidence">
                        <li class="box">
                            <strong>Evidence:</strong> the recorded facts, and every docket document
                            with readable text
                        </li>
                        <li class="box key">The guard: five checks</li>
                        <li class="box">The agent</li>
                    </ol>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <ol class="route" aria-label="Synthesis">
                        <li class="box">
                            <strong>Synthesis:</strong> the investigators' factual and analysis
                            write-ups
                        </li>
                        <li class="box held">Withheld, always</li>
                    </ol>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <ol class="route" aria-label="Verdict">
                        <li class="box">
                            <strong>Verdict:</strong> the probable cause, and the occurrence and
                            finding codes
                        </li>
                        <li class="box held">
                            Withheld until the agent has answered, then used for scoring
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </li>
        <li class="box">Scoring: the agent's answer against the verdict, by exact match</li>
    </ol>
    <figcaption>
        Every case passes through one function that divides it into three parts (decision{" "}
        <a href={d0013}>0013</a>). Only the evidence reaches the agent, and only after the guard.
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<h3>The guard's five checks</h3>
<ol class="checks">
    <li>
        <strong>Only declared fields are read.</strong> The evidence comes from a fixed list of
        places in the record, and from nowhere else.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>The evidence has a fixed shape.</strong> Nothing can be added to it on the way.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Nothing comes from a withheld part of the record.</strong> No evidence field may sit
        inside the write-ups, the probable cause or the coded events and findings. The one named
        exception is the phase of flight of the defining event, which an open case carries from its
        first day.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Every value is checked against its source.</strong> A test compares each value the
        agent would see with the place in the record it is declared to come from.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>A last check refuses the case.</strong> If the probable cause or any sentence of it,
        a whole write-up, or any of the case's codes appears in what the agent would see, the case
        is not shown to the agent at all. Docket documents and weather reports may repeat sentences
        of the factual write-up, which quotes them. A sentence shared with the analysis write-up
        only marks the case, and the mark never reaches the agent (decision <a href={d0077}>0077</a>
        ).
    </li>
</ol>
<p>
    No docket document is held back for its title: whether a document is evidence cannot be told
    from its title, so every readable document goes through the same checks. Tests break the split
    on purpose, with a value taken from the wrong place or a withheld sentence slipped into the
    evidence, and each must be caught (decision <a href={d0016}>0016</a>).
</p>

<style>
    .split {
        display: grid;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        margin: 0;
    }
    ol {
        list-style: none;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
    }
    .flow,
    .route {
        display: grid;
        gap: 1.4rem;
    }
    .box {
        position: relative;
        padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--ink-muted);
        border-radius: 4px;
        background: var(--ground);
    }
    .key {
        border-width: 2px;
        border-color: var(--ink);
    }
    .held {
        border-style: dashed;
        color: var(--ink-muted);
    }
    /* The arrow from each box to the next, drawn as a line and a head below it. */
    .flow > li:not(:last-child)::after,
    .route > li:not(:last-child)::after {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        left: 1.5rem;
        bottom: -1.4rem;
        height: 1.4rem;
        border-left: 2px solid var(--ink-muted);
    }
    .flow > li:not(.box):not(:last-child) {
        position: relative;
    }
    /* Each part is its own panel, so on a phone the three stacked routes never read as one chain. */
    .routes {
        display: grid;
        gap: 0.75rem;
    }
    .routes > li {
        padding: 0.75rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--rule);
        border-radius: 6px;
    }
    @media (min-width: 680px) {
        .routes {
            grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
            align-items: start;
        }
    }
    figcaption {
        color: var(--ink-muted);
    }
    .checks {
        display: grid;
        gap: 0.5rem;
        list-style: decimal;
        padding-left: 1.6rem;
    }
    h3 {
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    }
    p {
        margin-block: 0;
    }
</style>
